msgid "Supported Spring Data REST functionalities"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus currently supports a subset of Spring Data REST features, namely the "
"most useful and most commonly used features."
msgstr ""

msgid "What is supported"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The following sections describe the most important supported features of "
"Spring Data REST."
msgstr ""

msgid "Automatic REST endpoint generation"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Interfaces that extend any of the following Spring Data repositories get "
"automatically generated REST endpoints:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`org.springframework.data.repository.CrudRepository`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`org.springframework.data.repository.PagingAndSortingRepository`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`org.springframework.data.jpa.repository.JpaRepository`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Endpoints generated from the above repositories expose five common REST "
"operations:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`GET /fruits` - lists all entities or returns a page if "
"`PagingAndSortingRepository` or `JpaRepository` is used."
msgstr ""

msgid "`GET /fruits/:id` - returns an entity by ID."
msgstr ""

msgid "`POST /fruits` - creates a new entity."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`PUT /fruits/:id` - updates an existing entity or creates a new one with a "
"specified ID (if allowed by the entity definition)."
msgstr ""

msgid "`DELETE /fruits/:id` - deletes an entity by ID."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"There are two supported data types: `application/json` and `application/"
"hal+json`.\n"
"The former is used by default, but it is highly recommended to specify which "
"one you prefer with an `Accept` header."
msgstr ""

msgid "Exposing many entities"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If a database contains many entities, it might not be a great idea to return "
"them all at once.\n"
"`PagingAndSortingRepository` allows the `spring-data-rest` extension to "
"access data in chunks."
msgstr ""

msgid "So, you can extend the `PagingAndSortingRepository`:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Now the `GET /fruits` will accept three new query parameters: `sort`, `page` "
"and `size`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Query parameter"
msgstr ""

msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

msgid "Default value"
msgstr ""

msgid "Example values"
msgstr ""

msgid "`sort`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Sorts the entities that are returned by the list operation"
msgstr ""

msgid "\"\""
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`?sort=name` (ascending name), `?sort=name,-color` (ascending name and "
"descending color)"
msgstr ""

msgid "`page`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Zero indexed page number. Invalid value is interpreted as 0."
msgstr ""

msgid "0"
msgstr ""

msgid "0, 11, 100"
msgstr ""

msgid "`size`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Page size. Minimal accepted value is 1. Any lower value is interpreted as 1."
msgstr ""

msgid "20"
msgstr ""

msgid "1, 11, 100"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For paged responses, `spring-data-rest` also returns a set of link headers "
"that can be used to access other pages: first, previous, next and last."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Additionally, rather than extending both `PagingAndSortingRepository` and "
"`CrudRepository`, you can use `JpaRepository`, which is a higher-level "
"abstraction tailored for JPA. Since `JpaRepository` already extends both "
"`PagingAndSortingRepository` and `CrudRepository`, it can replace "
"`CrudRepository` directly."
msgstr ""

msgid "Fine tuning endpoints generation"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This allows user to specify which methods should be exposed and what path "
"should be used to access them.\n"
"Spring Data REST provides two annotations that can be used: "
"`@RepositoryRestResource` and `@RestResource`.\n"
"`spring-data-rest` extension supports the `exported`, `path` "
"`collectionResourceRel` attributes of these annotations."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Assume for example that fruits repository should be accessible by a `/my-"
"fruits` path and only allow `GET` operation.\n"
"In such a case, `FruitsRepository` would look like so:"
